change:
  id: CHG-018
  title: Aim each review brief at ground the previous passes did not examine
  status: proposed
  intent: Sharpen the existing different-briefs rule with the coverage reason CHG-016 demonstrated, so a decision about another review pass is made on unexamined region rather than on count.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - PAT-003
    - ARCH-001

deltas:
  - op: MODIFIED
    capability: review-and-consolidation-contract
    requirement: The contract directs each review brief at a region the previous passes did not examine, and PAT-003 records the evidence and the stopping condition.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: the repository contract is checked
        then: the independent review section requires aiming each brief at a region the previous passes did not examine
        and:
          - deleting that clause fails the check and names it
      - id: S2
        when: an agent decides whether another review pass is worth running
        then: PAT-003 gives the stopping condition, that the question is which region is still unexamined and not how many passes have run
        and:
          - it records the evidence as one change plus one corroborating instance, not as a law

acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: repo-contract/agents-review-consolidation-controls
    layer: contract
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: repo-contract/knowledge-pat-003-resolves
    layer: contract

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: sharpen the existing AGENTS.md clause rather than adding a section, and guard it
    status: completed
  - id: T2
    slice: record the CHG-016 evidence table and the stopping condition in PAT-003
    status: completed

non_goals:
  - requiring a fixed number of review passes
  - adding a new section for a rule that already has a home
  - promoting PAT-003 to canonical on two instances

risks:
  - two instances is not a law, and a heuristic stated in a guarded contract reads more settled than the evidence warrants. PAT-003 states the evidence base explicitly next to the claim
  - a stopping condition phrased as "no unexamined region remains" can be satisfied by asserting none remains. It is a prompt for judgement, not a test
